# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained / unsafe by design.
# Module-level advisory, UNKNOWN severity, NO fixed version — it flags every
# consumer of the x/crypto module regardless of which packages are imported.
# This repo does not import x/crypto/openpgp anywhere (grep the tree), and the
# call-graph-aware govulncheck gate (make vuln, CI "Vulnerability scan")
# remains the authoritative reachability check and stays green.
#
# The release gate (fixed CRITICAL/HIGH only) would not trip on this entry;
# the suppression exists to keep the non-gating all-severities report and any
# consumer's own `trivy image` scan free of this unactionable noise. Remove it
# if openpgp is ever imported or the advisory gains a fixed version.
GO-2026-5932
